<article class="env-lemma" id="0DX4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DX4">Lemma <span data-tag="0DX4">51.15.2</span>.</a> Let $j : U \to X$ be an open immersion of Noetherian schemes. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Assume $\mathcal{F}' = j_*(\mathcal{F}|_ U)$ is coherent. Then $\mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{F}'$ is the unique map of coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules such that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\mathcal{F}|_ U \to \mathcal{F}'|_ U$ is an isomorphism, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\text{depth}_{\mathcal{O}_{X, x}}(\mathcal{F}'_ x) \geq 2$ for $x \in X$, $x \not\in U$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> If $f : Y \to X$ is a flat morphism with $Y$ Noetherian, then $f^*\mathcal{F} \to f^*\mathcal{F}'$ is the corresponding map for $f^{-1}(U) \subset Y$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We have $\text{depth}_{\mathcal{O}_{X, x}}(\mathcal{F}'_ x) \geq 2$ by Divisors, Lemma <a href="/tag/0EY0" data-tag="0EY0">31.6.6</a> part (3). The uniqueness of $\mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{F}'$ follows from Divisors, Lemma <a href="/tag/0E9I" data-tag="0E9I">31.5.11</a>. The compatibility with flat pullbacks follows from flat base change, see Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/02KH" data-tag="02KH">30.5.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>